graph500 3.0.0 predates GCC 14, which promoted -Wimplicit-function-declaration
from a warning to an error (C99 removed implicit declarations; GCC 14 finally
enforces it).  Two call sites rely on implicit declarations:

  * src/bitmap_reference.h expands memset() in the CLEAN_VISITED() macro but
    never includes <string.h>.
  * src/main.c calls isisolated(), which is defined in src/csr_reference.c as
    "int isisolated(int64_t v)" but is never declared in a header.  The
    implicit declaration "int isisolated()" drops the int64_t parameter type,
    which is a real (if latent on x86-64 SysV) ABI mismatch.

Declare both properly instead of suppressing the diagnostic.

diff -Naur a/src/bitmap_reference.h b/src/bitmap_reference.h
--- a/src/bitmap_reference.h
+++ b/src/bitmap_reference.h
@@ -8,6 +8,8 @@
 /*           Andrew Lumsdaine                                              */
 /*           Anton Korzh                                                   */
 
+#include <string.h>
+
 #define ulong_bits 64
 #define ulong_mask &63
 #define ulong_shift >>6
diff -Naur a/src/common.h b/src/common.h
--- a/src/common.h
+++ b/src/common.h
@@ -207,6 +207,8 @@
 						void* xmalloc(size_t nbytes); /* In utils.c */
 						void* xcalloc(size_t n, size_t unit); /* In utils.c */
 
+						int isisolated(int64_t v); /* In csr_reference.c */
+
 						int validate_result(int isbfs, const tuple_graph* const tg, const size_t nlocalverts, const int64_t root, int64_t* const pred, float * dist, int64_t* const edge_visit_count_ptr); /* In validate.c */
 
